Cell[TextData[{
 "The fast-bath pair lies together: A1 recovered as a limit. The slow-bath \
pair splits everywhere: the constant-rate stand-in plunges at once and stays \
down, while the true curve starts flat, dies, and then partially revives as \
the auxiliary mode hands amplitude back, with the black points from the joint \
simulation riding the closed form. So A1 owns the exponential time profile \
and the monotonicity of decoherence. What it does not own is the separation \
dependence: the exponent is proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 " at every instant in both columns, because that factor comes from the \
overlap of Gaussian lobes, not from the bath's clock. The headline's ",
 StyleBox["scaling", "TI"],
 " needs less than the headline's ",
 StyleBox["curve", "TI"],
 ", and this cell is, to this file's knowledge, the first in this folder to \
exercise the memory assumption at all."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Raising the cutoff (A5).",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Recompute the extracted coherence at a fixed time across three truncations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"coherAt", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"run", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"evolveODE", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"0", " ", 
              RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "nn", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]cat", "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"annihilation", "[", "nn", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
             "       ", 
             RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", 
              RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"coherentState", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "\[Alpha]0"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                
                RowBox[{"coherentState", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"-", "\[Alpha]0"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
             " ", "0.8"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"catCoherence", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"run", "[", "0.8", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Alpha]0", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]cat"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"0.8", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"coherAt", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"22", ",", " ", "30", ",", " ", "38"}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->39707610,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
  "0.14521227826034921`", ",", "0.14521229939299185`", ",", 
   "0.14521230966832882`"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[34]= ",
 CellID->76238682,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The three values agree at the displayed precision: the truncation is not what \
any conclusion above rests on.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell["The list, after the computations", "Subsection",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The list the computations leave behind is shorter and sharper than the list \
we wrote. A3 is gone: a free drive rotates the picture rigidly and changes \
nothing, so it was never an assumption, only a simplification, with the \
recorded boundary that the Hamiltonian must keep coherent states coherent. A4 \
split into three scopes: the formula never needed it, the headline is nothing \
but it, and the extraction machinery fails without it. C1 turned out to be \
innocent exactly inside A4 and guilty outside it, so the choice of coherence \
number and the separation assumption travel together. A2 owns the prefactor \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " and the identity of the pointer states. A1 owns the exponential profile \
and the monotonicity, but not the separation-squared scaling, which survives \
even a bath that hands amplitude back. What began as five facts and a choice \
ends as: linearity of the loss gives the scaling, A1 gives the clock, A2 \
gives the prefactor, A4 gives the phenomenon."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell["Part Two: Rapid Purification, Rebuilt from Its Assumptions", "Section",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell["The questions, weakest premises first", "Subsection",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Q1.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Does continuously watching one observable, with no drive and no feedback, \
purify a single monitored run? (This needs the least: one qubit, one measured \
channel, a kept record.)"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Q2.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " What sets the purification rate, and can choosing ",
 StyleBox["what to measure", "TI"],
 ", step by step, make the rate certain, the same on every record?"
}], "Text",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Q3.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Is \"faster\" one question? Two scores are in circulation, the average \
impurity at a deadline and the typical time to reach a target, and nothing \
guarantees they rank two protocols the same way."
}], "Text",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Q4.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Which assumptions carry these answers: what changes when a drive rotates \
the qubit, when the detector misses a fraction of the record, when a second \
channel goes unwatched, when the time step is finite?"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell["The words, defined by computation", "Subsection",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell["\<\
The qubit objects first, the Pauli matrices and the Bloch vector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}], " ", 
   "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "j", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"impurity", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "rho", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], 
    "/", "2"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Impurity",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is the score: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptL]", "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 " for Bloch vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],
 ", one half for the maximally mixed state and zero for a pure one. It is the \
same information as the purity, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptL]", "=", "1", "-", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 "; check the identity on an arbitrary state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.7", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0.2", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.1", " ", "I"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"0.2", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.1", " ", "I"}]}], ",", " ", "0.3"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"impurity", "[", "rho", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"purity", "[", "rho", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->1375306244,ExpressionUUID->"0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"0.31999999999999995`", ",", "0.32000000000000006`"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[36]= ",
 CellID->434954992,ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The two numbers agree. Using impurity rather than entropy is a choice, so \
prove the choice harmless rather than assert it: for a qubit the von Neumann \
entropy is a strictly increasing function of the impurity, so the two scores \
rank any two states identically and reach any target in the same order:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"vnEntropy", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ev", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
           RowBox[{"N", "@", "rho"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", " ", ">", " ", 
           RowBox[{"10", "^", 
            RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ev", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Log", "[", "ev", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"r", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"vnEntropy", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"id2", " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"r", " ", "Z"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "0.999", ",", " ", "0.001", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "0.002"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<impurity\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<von Neumann entropy\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<one score is a monotone relabeling of the other\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->1021162360,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

