Cell["\<\
The fixed-axis times spread wide, with a lucky early crowd and a slow tail; \
the steered times bunch at one value, because determinism forbids luck in \
both directions. So Q3's answer: \"which is faster\" is not one question. \
Under the deadline score steering wins; under the race score the fixed axis \
wins; and any essay claiming one protocol \"purifies faster\" without naming \
its score has not said anything yet. This is the same lesson as Gaussian \
versus thermal, now about an adverb.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1009200201,ExpressionUUID->"621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],

Cell["Turning the assumptions off", "Subsection",
 CellID->752465254,ExpressionUUID->"5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Switch the drive on (B1 off).",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Add a Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 " and rerun both protocols. For the steered one nothing should change: the \
re-aiming reads the state after each step, so a known rotation between steps \
is absorbed by the next choice of axis, and the deterministic law should \
survive. For the fixed axis the drive should ",
 StyleBox["help", "TI"],
 ": the slow tail came from runs stuck aligned with the measured axis, and a \
rotation keeps pulling the state away from alignment, where the measurement \
learns fastest. First the fixed axis, driven against undriven, with the \
steered mean for scale:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->891183881,ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"grid", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"hPur", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "200"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"meanDrive", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"impurity", " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"1.5", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "kPur", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", 
             " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "hPur", ",", " ", "2.", ",", " ", 
             "s"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "100"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"grid", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "unsteeredEns", "]"}], ",", " ", "201"}], 
           "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"grid", ",", " ", "meanDrive"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"grid", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "steeredEns", "]"}], ",", " ", "201"}], 
